--- Stage 11 floor-accept diagnostics and internal cooldown ---
The native `ExecSimulation` adaptive state also contains:

     INTEGER :: AdaptiveRejectedBeforeAccept, AdaptiveCooldownBeforeAccept, &
          AdaptiveGrowthCooldownRemaining
     REAL(KIND=dp) :: AdaptiveAcceptedDt, AdaptivePreviousDtBeforeAccept, &
          AdaptiveProposedNextDt, AdaptiveAppliedGrowthFactor
     REAL(KIND=dp), PARAMETER :: AdaptivePostRejectMaxGrowth = 1.2_dp

Before the acceptance test it records `dt_is_min`, `ordinary_error`,
`forced_floor`, the previous rejection streak, and the pre-accept `h_old`.
After acceptance it emits `Adaptive accept`, `Adaptive accept ratio`,
`Adaptive accept flags`, `Adaptive accept cooldown`, and `Adaptive accept
growth` records when debugging or recovering from a reject.

The acceptance growth decision is:

     IF ( AdaptiveForcedFloor ) THEN
       ddt = AdaptiveMinTimestep
       AdaptiveGrowthCooldownRemaining = 1
     ELSE IF ( AdaptiveGrowthCooldownRemaining > 0 ) THEN
       ddt = MIN( AdaptivePostRejectMaxGrowth * ddt, AdaptiveMaxTimeStep )
       AdaptiveGrowthCooldownRemaining = AdaptiveGrowthCooldownRemaining - 1
     ELSE
       ddt = MIN( AdaptiveIncrease * ddt, AdaptiveMaxTimeStep )
     END IF

Rejection sets `AdaptiveGrowthCooldownRemaining = 1`. This is an internal
policy default; no new SIF keyword is required.
